# Shell scripts MUST stay LF, even on Windows (core.autocrlf=true).
# A CRLF shebang (`#!/bin/bash\r`) makes a git hook fail with "bad interpreter",
# which would BLOCK commits instead of failing open -- see scripts/precommit-build-guard.sh
# and scripts/install-hooks.sh. Pinning eol=lf prevents that on fresh clones.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Git hooks in .githooks/ have no extension, so the *.sh rule above does not cover them.
# A CRLF shebang fails with "bad interpreter" and blocks commits.
/.githooks/pre-commit text eol=lf
/.githooks/post-commit text eol=lf

# Batch wrappers MUST stay CRLF -- the mirror image of the rule above.
# cmd.exe reads a .bat by byte offset assuming CRLF; with LF-only endings the
# seek arithmetic drifts and it executes lines with the first character eaten
# (`REM` -> `M`, `setlocal` -> `etlocal`). Verified 2026-07-25 under `cmd /c`:
# the same 53-line wrapper fails as LF and succeeds as CRLF.
#
# The failure is content/size dependent, so it is LATENT -- short wrappers work
# fine as LF, which is exactly what makes it dangerous: it surfaces later, as
# garbled execution rather than a clean error, in an unattended scheduled task.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Node scripts stay LF. 204 of them start with a shebang, and vitest cannot import a module whose
# shebang line ends in \r ("SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected token"); node can. Every tracked
# .mjs/.js/.cjs is already LF in the index, so this changes checkouts only. Keep it above the
# vendored rule so _vendor stays -text.
*.mjs text=auto eol=lf
*.js text=auto eol=lf
*.cjs text=auto eol=lf

# Test fixtures (captured review bodies, JSON) stay LF. Tests cut them apart on "\n"; a CRLF
# checkout made 9 review-status Follow-up tests fail on Windows only (2026-11-02, after #245).
/scripts/github/fixtures/** text eol=lf

# Vendored external skills stay byte-identical to upstream (core.autocrlf=true would rewrite them
# and break the per-file sha256 in vendor.lock.json). Spec: docs/self-improvement/proposals/2026-10-02-skill-intake-fabric.md.
.claude/skills/_vendor/** -text

# Hook sources stay LF. The freshness manifest hashes LF bytes; a CRLF checkout
# would otherwise differ in all 149 sources (dist-freshness.ts also strips CR).
/.claude/hooks/src/**/*.ts text eol=lf

# Always-loaded instruction files stay LF: the context budget counts every \r, so CRLF costs
# ~377 chars (scripts/rules/context-budget-guard.mjs; 2026-10-03 trim pass).
/.claude/templates/CLAUDE.md.template text eol=lf
/.claude/rules-src/on-demand-rules.md text eol=lf
/CLAUDE.md text eol=lf
/CONTEXT.md text eol=lf
/AGENTS.md text eol=lf
